{
  "id": "PPA-13",
  "title": "Phloem Vasculature Sucrose & Nutrient Transport",
  "subtitle": "Source minor vein apoplastic/symplastic loading, sieve tube M\u00fcnch pressure flow, and sink unloading",
  "caption": "Long-distance vasculature sucrose and nutrient partitioning (PMM-11). Connects chloroplast photosynthetic carbon fixation in mature source leaves to heterotrophic sink respiration in roots. In source minor veins, sucrose is exported into the apoplast by SWEET11/12/15 uniporters and actively concentrated into companion cells by the SUC2/SUT1 H+-symporter energized by AHA3 (or symplastically trapped via GOLS/RFS raffinose polymers). Hydrostatic pressure drives sap flow through sieve tubes guarded by CalS7 callose collars and SEOR1/2 filaments. In sink roots, sucrose is unloaded apoplastically via CWINV1/2/4 and STP1/4/13 hexose symporters, or cleaved symplastically by SUS1/4 to fuel mitochondrial respiration.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
